Implement three runtime error handling fixes:

1. Fix 1: Global Express error handler (api/src/app.ts):
```typescript
// Add at end of app.ts, after all routes:
app.use((err: any, req: express.Request, res: express.Response, next: express.NextFunction) => {
  console.error('Unhandled error:', err);
  res.status(err.status || 500).json({
    success: false,
    error: {
      code: err.code || 'INTERNAL_ERROR',
      message: err.message || 'An unexpected error occurred',
    },
  });
});
```
   - User impact: Prevents HTML error pages in frontend; consistent JSON error format
   - Reproduction: Trigger unhandled error (e.g., uncaught exception in route)
   - Before: Frontend gets HTML 500 page, chokes parsing
   - After: Frontend gets JSON `{ success: false, error: {...} }`

2. Fix 2: WebSocket session mid-connection re-check (api/src/collaboration/index.ts):
```typescript
// Add periodic session validation in message handler:
const SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS = 60000; // 1 minute
let lastSessionCheck = Date.now();

ws.on('message', async (data) => {
  if (Date.now() - lastSessionCheck > SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS) {
    const session = await validateSession(cookies);
    if (!session || session.expired) {
      ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'error', message: 'Session expired, please reload' }));
      ws.close();
      return;
    }
    lastSessionCheck = Date.now();
  }
  // ... existing message handling
});
```
   - User impact: Session expiry during editing now disconnects with clear message
   - Reproduction: Open document, wait 16 minutes, edit (session expired but WS still open)
   - Before: Edits silently fail or persist beyond timeout
   - After: User sees "Session expired, please reload" toast and WS disconnects

3. Fix 3: yjsToJson() safety wrap (api/src/collaboration/index.ts:118):
```typescript
// Wrap yjsToJson() call with try/catch and fallback:
try {
  const contentJson = yjsToJson(ydoc);
  if (!contentJson || typeof contentJson !== 'object') {
    throw new Error('Invalid content JSON');
  }
  await db.query(
    'UPDATE documents SET content = $1 WHERE id = $2',
    [contentJson, docId]
  );
} catch (error) {
  console.error('yjsToJson failed, using last known content:', error);
  // Fallback: don't update content column if conversion fails
  // Or: fetch last-known-good content from document_history
}
```
   - User impact: Prevents silent content corruption when JSON snapshot fails
   - Reproduction: Trigger yjsToJson failure (malformed Yjs state)
   - Before: content column set to string "undefined", data loss
   - After: content preserved, error logged, fallback to last-known-good

4. Document before/after with screenshots/recordings in orientation/improvements/runtime-error-handling.md

Target: 3 fixes, ≥1 addressing user-visible data loss/confusion
